Lab: Implementing Enterprise Integration Patterns with Apache Camel
Objectives
By the end of this lab, you will be able to:

Implement the Content-Based Router pattern to route order messages to different processing paths based on message content
Apply the Splitter pattern to break a batch of orders into individual messages for independent processing
Apply the Aggregator pattern to combine related order messages back into a single grouped result, persisted to a file for verification
Configure and wire Apache Camel routes using Java DSL inside a Spring Boot application
Test each pattern with curl and verify correct behavior from application logs and a persisted output file
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, you should have:

Basic understanding of Java programming
Familiarity with the Maven build tool
Understanding of REST APIs, HTTP, and JSON
Basic command-line skills
Required tools (install if not already present):

java -version    # requires OpenJDK 11 or later
mvn -version     # requires Maven 3.8+
curl --version
If any of these are missing, install them with your system package manager, for example:

sudo apt-get update && sudo apt-get install -y openjdk-11-jdk maven curl
