Troubleshooting
Aggregation never completes / no file appears: check that completionTimeout(10000) has elapsed if you sent fewer than 3 orders of the same customerType, and confirm the customerId header is being set correctly from jsonpath("$.customerType") before reaching the aggregator.
BUILD FAILURE mentioning jsonpath: confirm the camel-jsonpath-starter dependency was added to pom.xml exactly as shown, then rerun mvn clean compile.
Conclusion
In this lab, you built a single Spring Boot application that implements three core Enterprise Integration Patterns with Apache Camel: a Content-Based Router that inspects order fields to choose a processing path, a Splitter that decomposes a batch order into individual messages and feeds them back through that same router, and an Aggregator that groups related orders by customer type, completes on either a size or time trigger, and persists the resulting summary to disk for verification. Through the curl-based tests you confirmed each pattern's behavior directly from log output and from the generated files in data/aggregated-orders/, reinforcing how these patterns route, decompose, and recombine messages in a realistic integration scenario. As a next step, consider extending the aggregator to write structured JSON instead of plain text, or adding a Dead Letter Channel to handle malformed order payloads gracefully.
